Draft:
Cyber actors have targeted critical infrastructure (CI) and internet-accessible operational technology (OT) assets. The sectors affected include the Defense Industrial Base (DIB) and National Security Systems (NSS). The primary motivation behind these actions is to cause harm to U.S. interests or retaliate for perceived U.S. aggression. Immediate measures are necessary to mitigate the impact of these activities. The U.S. government recommends that entities immediately secure OT assets and ensure the resilience and safety of U.S. systems. This will help prevent further exploitation and reduce the risk of disruptions to critical infrastructure and operations. Effective implementation of these measures will require a coordinated effort among all stakeholders to ensure the continued security and stability of U.S. systems and networks.

