TrickBot operators have been observed employing various tactics to compromise systems. Utilizing the Man in the Browser technique [T1185], the actors enable themselves to intercept and manipulate sensitive information. Additionally, the operators conduct reconnaissance [TA0043] to gather intelligence on target systems. The ultimate goal of these activities is to impact systems and data, enabling the TrickBot operators to steal information, manipulate, interrupt, or destroy systems and data. Organizations are advised to apply best practices to strengthen the security posture of their systems and review any configuration changes prior to implementation to mitigate the threat posed by TrickBot malware. Effective implementation of these mitigations is crucial in preventing potential system disruptions.

